      "source_quote": "Consider the harlot Rahab.",
      "suggested_fix": "The translation uses “mke haramu Rahabu.” That is understandable but nonstandard Swahili Bible usage commonly renders her name as “Rahabu” (with final -u is acceptable) and the phrase for “the harlot” is typically “msichana wa mizinga” or “mchawi” is wrong — keep a clear, neutral phrase. Suggest keeping “Rahabu” and using the more neutral “mke wa mali mtakatifu” is incorrect. Recommended minimal change: use “Mademu Rahabu” or simply “Rahabu” with context preserved. Example suggested wording (Swahili): “Fikiria Rahabu, msichana wa mizinga.”",
      "translation_quote": "Fikiria juu ya mke haramu Rahabu."
